WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.050
- People have been getting tattoos

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.613
since day one for a reason.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.513
Some do it for expression and identity.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.450
Some do it just because it's cool

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.870
which in my mind is just as valid.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.580
Some people use them as mementos

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.505
and others get tattoos
to heal painful memories.

00:00:33.297 --> 00:00:34.130
Come here, come on.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.550
My name is Brian Finn.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.253
I've been tattooing for 20
years here in Toledo, Ohio.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.357
Alexa, ask Delta to fill dog bowl.

00:00:43.357 --> 00:00:45.600
(water splashing)

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.300
I think what I like most about tattooing

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.330
and what drew me to it was the freedom.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.100
In 2015, I decided that
I was gonna come in

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.500
on of my days off

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.030
and tattoo over scars that were
caused by human trafficking,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.023
self-harm, and domestic violence.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.340
- I wouldn't be who I am
today without my past.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.600
I started cutting when I was 17.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.190
I felt like it was the only way

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.180
to feel things sometimes
when I had numbed myself

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.300
to the point where I
wasn't feeling anything.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.560
It got really bad in my early 20s

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.420
and that's when most
of these scars are from

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:25.170
that will be tattooed over today.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.190
- I think that I'm helping people

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.660
by finishing that chapter in their lives.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:32.990
They can go onto the next.

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:34.870
They don't have a daily reminder.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.620
Alexa, ask Delta to fill one cup.

00:01:39.573 --> 00:01:42.406
(water whooshing)

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.640
- I think I'm really getting
to a place in my life

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.360
where I'm moving past those things

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.582
and really comfortable with who I am

00:01:50.582 --> 00:01:53.499
and I'm comfortable in my own skin.

00:01:54.576 --> 00:01:56.493
- Alrighty, here we go.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.910
- I think that having the
dragonfly on my forearm

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:04.680
will help remind me that
I have built this future

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.820
for myself and I have
transformed and I am realizing

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.030
who I'm meant to be

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.530
and I think that it will
help by covering the scars

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.760
to avoid that trigger a little bit,

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.693
that feeling of wanting the pain again.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:20.170
It's about building more positive memories

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.512
and building a life worth living.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.480
Dragonflies symbolize transformation

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.360
and self realization.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.880
I'm building on the past
and building a new life

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.800
for myself and transforming
and something beautiful

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.717
can grow from the pain.

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:55.260
- I think I choose to take the time

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.093
to help people out

00:02:56.093 --> 00:02:57.640
because a lot of people
don't take the time

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:58.590
to help people out.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.820
So, anyone that is looking for a tattoo

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.739
for whatever reason, I'll be here.

